# Double-click takes a word, triple-click takes the line.
#
# The band itself is a drawn rectangle and invisible to a text assertion, so
# the composer's "N selected" readout is what makes the selection observable —
# which is also why it exists: a short highlight behind text is easy to miss.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

expect_no_text selected

# Inside "ledger" on the first account line: six characters.
# The y here is a measured text-line centre, not a guess -- the three body
# lines sit at 209 / 225 / 241. They were at 226 / 242 / 258 until the hover
# Copy row stopped being reserved in the layout (feat/vis-fixture: it is an
# overlay on the bubble now, as Puffin's is), which lifted every reply by 24px
# and then put 10 back as turn air and 4 as the transcript's top inset. They
# were at 184 / 200 / 216 before that, until the thread began on a user turn (a
# right-aligned bubble and its avatar, to match Puffin's reference frame). A
# coordinate click is brittle by nature (see afterhours_gaps.md: there is no
# way to ask where a piece of text landed), so if this starts selecting the
# wrong word, re-measure rather than nudge -- render t2 at this script's own
# 1100x760 and scan the PNG for the bubble's band.
double_click 415 225
wait_frames 6
expect_text "6 selected"

# The whole line is much longer than one word.
triple_click 415 225
wait_frames 6
expect_no_text "6 selected"
expect_text "61 selected"

# A press on empty space drops it.
click 700 300
wait_frames 6
expect_no_text selected
